  "interpretation": {
    "four_noses": "Four projecting rectangular returns on each outer side, with another two fine beads between adjacent steps. The broad soffit covers the entire upper bay.",
    "central_spandrel": "Two vertical boundaries of the centre strip in photo 08 lie near (679,345) and (737,405), approximately −.27 and +.31m in the external frame. Modelling width .181 of the bay width. The little beads in the flutes are represented by three shallow profiles.",
    "opening_measurement": "The lower second-storey sash is behind the steps, set on the original street wall; the two street mobilizations are measured separately by the main-building author. A three-light sash is directly visible below the slab. Upper glass is behind each projected plaster face.",
    "limits": "2015/2020街面上有线缆、树枝及个别开扇，两个街翼的横梃和原饰边有修缮期差异。肋、钢材与凹灰面按近景明暗概括。约3.05m的宽度取自两街面联合定尺，绝对挑深仍为由单照和该宽推算的估计。四步净宽与落差相对关系有较好约束。",
    "fourth_and_fifth_floor_sills": "Fourth floor top/bottom heights at the two street openings derive from 2015: approximately 11.92–12.12 / 10.32–10.61 m. Fifth: 15.38–15.68 / 13.71–14.07 m. Horizontal wires are not glazing bars; the underlying fourth, fifth rows have two steel mullions and one crossbar."
  },
  "photo_edge_explanation": "Near the third-floor glazing, the observed horizontal steel rail crosses the second upright at about (712,89). The short visible right leaf terminates near (766,182); (773,175) falls within its right jamb / masonry return. Photo 08 was cropped in-camera across the roofward part of this window. This framing was read independently of the two whole-building street photographs."
}
